            <ArticleTitle>Sequence of occurrence of abnormal regional cardiac function, global pump function and electrocardiogram after brief ligation and reperfusion of a coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1059-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The following results were obtained. During brief ligation of the coronary artery, a change in the cardiac wall motion appeared as the first abnormality of the CMG. Succeedingly, epicardial ECG changes were recognized, and lastly, changes of dP/dt appeared. After reperfusion of the coronary artery, dP/dt was quickly normalized, followed by restoration of ST elevation. Cardiac motion, measured by CMG, was the last abnormality to improve.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
